---
/**
 * Active Layers panel (ATLAS-1205 / KAN-401).
 *
 * Discovery and composition are different tasks. Once several layers are on, a
 * reader should not have to remember which accordion, Room or collection each
 * one came from in order to take it off again.
 *
 * The panel owns no state. It renders from the canonical active-layer set and
 * writes back through the same checkboxes the browser uses, so the browser, the
 * panel and MapLibre cannot disagree about what is drawn.
 *
 * A layer that falls outside the selected year stays in the composition and is
 * marked, never silently dropped: the year moved, the reader's intent did not.
 */
---

<section class="aal" data-active-layers hidden>
  <div class="aal-head">
    <h3>
      Active layers
      <span class="aal-count" data-active-count>0</span>
    </h3>
    <button type="button" class="aal-clear" data-active-clear>Clear all</button>
  </div>
  <ul class="aal-list" data-active-list></ul>
  <p class="aal-note" data-active-note hidden>
    A layer outside the selected year keeps its place here. Move the year or remove it.
  </p>
</section>
